      "code": "LABEL_ERROR",
      "text": "Any attempt to infer 'offensive reorganization' from play-by-play data (e.g., shifts in play types, player roles, or initiation patterns) will likely rely on labels that are either inferred or inherently noisy. Historical evidence (FAM:SF-APPA-005, FAM:SF-APPM-021, FAM:SF38) consistently highlights the risk of label error making it hard to distinguish true reorganization from measurement artifact."
