    "controls": "Control for opponent defensive rating, game state (score differential, quarter), home/away, other concurrent player absences, and prior offensive efficiency (PPP in 'L' spell). Use within-team comparisons to control for team-level fixed effects. Consider matching spell pairs rigorously.",
    "falsification": "A falsification test could involve applying the 'reorganization' measurement to situations where no player absence occurred, expecting to see no significant 'reorganization' or no predictive relationship with PPP change. Also, test the reliability of the 'reorganization' measure and 'change in PPP' using split-half correlations or similar methods, expecting to find low reliability based on historical evidence (FAM:SF-CHT-064).",
